## Why This Is Asked
Realistic sprint planning with bounded weekly windows; tests ability to form and optimize DP with small constant branching and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for fast range totals
- DP with fixed window length (2..7)
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time O(n) with a small constant, Space O(n)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minWeeklyCost(A, W) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const INF = 1e18;
  const dp = new Array(n+1).fill(INF);
  const par = new Array(n+1).fill(-1);
  dp[0] = 0;
  for (let i=2; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let k=2; k<=7; k++) {
      if (i-k < 0) break;
      const sum = pref[i] - pref[i-k];
      const cost = dp[i-k] + (sum - W)*(sum - W);
      if (cost < dp[i]) { dp[i] = cost; par[i] = i-k; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would follow using par[]
  return {cost: dp[n], prev: par[n]};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negative A values if allowed? 
- What changes if weeks must start on a specific weekday?

## Why This Is Asked
Models practical scheduling under capacity with a convex (squared) day cost, exercising 2D DP and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and days
- Transition constrained by daily capacity D
- Prefix sums for O(1) range sums
- Backtracking via parent pointers to recover daily blocks
- Complexity: O(n^2 m) time, O(n m) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostSchedule(A, m, D) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] + A[i - 1];
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let d = 1; d <= m; d++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        const sum = pref[i] - pref[j];
        if (sum <= D && dp[j][d - 1] !== INF) {
          const cost = dp[j][d - 1] + sum * sum;
          if (cost < dp[i][d]) {
            dp[i][d] = cost;
            par[i][d] = j;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  if (dp[n][m] === INF) return { cost: -1, blocks: [] };
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, d = m;
  while (d > 0) {
    const j = par[i][d];
    blocks.push([j + 1, i]);
    i = j;
    d--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { cost: dp[n][m], blocks };
}
```

